{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:0d13a1c3c7f04e82","name":"Dreadnaught-Class Heavy Cruiser","source":{"id":"source:reference-0d13a1c3c7f04e82","title":"Dreadnaught-Class Heavy Cruiser","revision":18691,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:33:53Z","sha256":"128fc3cc7c419d6699ec91a5363c8adf986aabf802fe4962f9a2f820d7bb8e1f","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18691","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Dreadnaught-Class%20Heavy%20Cruiser&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-0d13a1c3c7f04e82","blocks":["\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["Vehicle Templates\n",{"tag":"p","children":["\n"]},"\n"],"colspan":2}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":[" Archaic Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Archaic_Dreadnaught-Class_Heavy_Cruiser","referenceId":"reference:510db34b5b772db7"},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["\n"]},"\n"],"colspan":2}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":[" Prototype Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Prototype_Dreadnaught-Class_Heavy_Cruiser","referenceId":"reference:a6206c2748a07a73"},"\n"],"colspan":2}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Designed by Rendili StarDrive in the waning days of the Republic, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruiser is a heavily armed battleship that remains in active use despite being supplanted by superior technologies. The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruiser came into service well before the beginning of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", but by the time the conflict arrived it had already become outdated. The newer ships, developed specifically for galaxywide warfare, quickly outstripped the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruiser in both power and reliability, but despite this fact the bulky heavy cruiser was a mainstay of the Republic fleet.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["During ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", most ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruisers were operated by volunteers or planetary defense forces, not clones. The high number of crewmembers required to operate a ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruiser made it a huge drain on personnel; however, the Republic chose to man these ships with volunteers, reserving their more advanced ships for their specially trained clone units and highly loyal officers. The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruiser continues to be found in service all throughout the galaxy; though the ship is considered antiqued at best, it boasts an armament that, despite its age, is not to be trifled with.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruiser's lack of shielding (compared to more cutting-edge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},", such as the ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Imperial I"]},"-Class Star Destroyer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Imperial_I-Class_Star_Destroyer","referenceId":"reference:3ceed6afca222030"},") is offset by its general toughness, meaning that if a shot gets through, it is less likely to reduce the ship's capabilities even if it destroys a large chunk of the ship. Most ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruisers were built with multiple redundant systems, allowing them to fight on despite suffering serve hits to certain parts of the ship.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As a result, many ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruisers are used as shields to protect more delicate ships, soaking up damage that would devastate a smaller vessel. The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruiser's smaller size (compared to the ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Imperial I"]},"-Class Star Destroyer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Imperial_I-Class_Star_Destroyer","referenceId":"reference:3ceed6afca222030"}," and its ilk) makes it less intimidating than other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},", but its sturdiness and reliability more than compensates for this drawback.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruiser Statistics (CL 18)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal (Cruiser) ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -4; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 13 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://sws